 Write a difference between for loop and for each loop.
 For loop provides index-based access and control, while for-each loop is used for simple traversal without index handling.
 
Feature	for loop	for-each loop
-Index access	    -Uses index (i) to access elements	Does not provide index
-Best used for	  	-When index control or modification is needed	When only reading elements
-Applicable on	  	-Arrays and collections	Arrays and collections
-Modification	  	-Can modify elements using index	Cannot modify structure directly
-Syntax	More flexible but verbose	-Simple and readable
 

